---
---

<figure class="resource-asset-diagram">
  <div class="layer">
    <header>
      <span class="kind">Your app table</span>
      <code>documents</code>
    </header>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">id</th>
            <th scope="col">title</th>
            <th scope="col">resource_id</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>doc_1</code></td>
            <td>Q3 report</td>
            <td><code>res_1</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>doc_2</code></td>
            <td>Q3 report copy</td>
            <td><code>res_2</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="layer-note">
      Query this table directly. Pagination, sorting, filtering, and joins stay in your control.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="connector">
    <span>references by <code>resource_id</code></span>
  </div>

  <div class="layer">
    <header>
      <span class="kind">Suitcase table</span>
      <code>resources</code>
    </header>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">id</th>
            <th scope="col">kind</th>
            <th scope="col">asset_id</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>res_1</code></td>
            <td>report</td>
            <td><code>asset_1</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>res_2</code></td>
            <td>report</td>
            <td><code>asset_1</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="connector">
    <span>both point at the same <code>asset_id</code></span>
  </div>

  <div class="layer">
    <header>
      <span class="kind">Suitcase table</span>
      <code>assets</code>
    </header>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">id</th>
            <th scope="col">hash</th>
            <th scope="col">bucket</th>
            <th scope="col">key</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>asset_1</code></td>
            <td><code>sha256:9f2c…</code></td>
            <td><code>documents</code></td>
            <td><code>reports/q3.pdf</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="layer-note">
      Suitcase manages the resources and assets rows through its persistence adapters. Treat them
      as library-managed state.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="connector">
    <span>
      <code>bucket</code> and <code>key</code> locate one object in the adapter
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="layer">
    <header>
      <span class="kind">Storage adapter</span>
      <code>documents bucket</code>
    </header>
    <div class="storage-object">
      <svg
        class="object-icon"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M6 2h8l4 4v16H6z"></path>
        <path d="M14 2v4h4"></path>
        <path d="M9 12h6M9 16h6"></path>
      </svg>
      <div class="object-body">
        <code class="object-key">reports/q3.pdf</code>
        <span class="object-meta">1.2 MB · sha256:9f2c…</span>
      </div>
      <span class="object-adapter">S3StorageBucket</span>
    </div>
    <p class="layer-note">
      The asset row stores the bucket and key, not the bytes. The storage adapter maps that pair to
      the physical object, signs reads, and removes it when the last reference is purged.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Two resources share one asset because the files have the same content hash. The asset stores the
    bucket and key, so one physical object backs both resources.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .resource-asset-diagram {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--card) 65%, transparent);
  }

  .layer {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .layer header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .kind {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .layer header code {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .layer-note {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .storage-object {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 80%, transparent);
    border-radius: calc(var(--radius) - 2px);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--background) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .object-icon {
    width: 1.5rem;
    height: 1.5rem;
    flex: none;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .object-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .object-key {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .object-meta {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
  }

  .object-adapter {
    margin-left: auto;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .layer table {
    display: table;
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .layer th {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: left;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .layer td {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 60%, transparent);
    color: var(--foreground);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .layer tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .layer td code,
  .layer th code {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .connector {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .connector span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .connector code {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .connector::after {
    content: "↓";
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .resource-asset-diagram {
      padding: 0.75rem;
    }

    .layer table {
      font-size: 0.6875rem;
    }

    .storage-object {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .object-adapter {
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
